  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Hiring a Kitchen Countertop Installer: What to Check in the Scope Before You Sign",
    "text": "Hiring a Kitchen Countertop Installer: What to Check in the Scope Before You Sign",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Are you reviewing an estimate for new kitchen surfaces and wondering what should actually be included? A common surprise during kitchen remodels is discovering that the quote only covers setting the slab, leaving you scrambling to find someone for the remaining tasks.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n\nTo protect your kitchen and budget, confirm whether your quote includes leveling the base cabinets, cutting openings for drop-in or undermount sinks, and handling cooktop clearances. Clarify upfront who manages disconnecting and reconnecting water lines, faucets, and garbage disposals. You should also ask where seams will fall, since slab size, transport access, and heavy material handling dictate seam placement. If you need tile backsplash work or drywall touch-ups around new overhangs, verify whether those trades are part of the agreement.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\nHeavy materials like stone or thick slabs require rigid, level cabinet bases and specialized structural support for overhangs. Overlooking uneven frames can cause cracking under load. Working with an experienced finish contractor ensures that sub-trade plumbing connections and cabinet leveling are handled properly from day one. Reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen countertop installation scope.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}